module

public import Sheaf.RingTheory.ProjectiveConeHilbertStandardDegrees
public import Sheaf.RingTheory.LocalStandardBasisInvariants
public import Sheaf.RingTheory.FormallyEtaleAssociatedGraded
public import WeilConjectures.RingTheory.IsRegularSystemOfParameters
import WeilConjectures.RingTheory.RegularLocalGeneratorsRegularSequence
import Mathlib.RingTheory.LocalRing.Quotient
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Noetherian.Basic

/-! # Linear sections and tangent-generator degrees

Source: Hironaka, Certain numerical characters of singularities (1970),
Propositions 5--6, pp.157--159, Lemma 7, p.160, and Remark (12.2), p.167
(blueprint: lem-trf-linear-sections-hilbert-standard-degrees).

The functions and initial ideals reuse the published Hironaka definitions. The additive
isomorphism is specified on every representative by the canonical graded quotient map;
its scalar and grading compatibility are included explicitly.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

namespace Hironaka

/-- The ideal generated by the displayed linear-section parameters.
Source: Hironaka (1970), Remark (12.2), p.167
(blueprint: lem-trf-linear-sections-hilbert-standard-degrees). -/
def linearSectionIdeal {V : Type u} [CommRing V] [IsLocalRing V] {q : ℕ}
    (x : Fin q → IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V) : Ideal V :=
  Ideal.span (Set.range fun i ↦ (x i).val)

/-- The actual quotient by the parameters; no local structure is chosen here.
Source: Hironaka (1970), Lemma 7 and Remark (12.2)
(blueprint: lem-trf-linear-sections-hilbert-standard-degrees). -/
abbrev linearSectionRing {V : Type u} [CommRing V] [IsLocalRing V] {q : ℕ}
    (x : Fin q → IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V) : Type u :=
  V ⧸ linearSectionIdeal x

/-- The image of the ambient maximal ideal in the parameter quotient.
Source: Hironaka (1970), Lemma 7, p.160
(blueprint: lem-trf-linear-sections-hilbert-standard-degrees). -/
def linearSectionMaximalIdeal {V : Type u} [CommRing V] [IsLocalRing V] {q : ℕ}
    (x : Fin q → IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V) : Ideal (linearSectionRing x) :=
  (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (linearSectionIdeal x))

/-- The canonical map on tangent cones is the published map on associated graded rings.
Source: Hironaka (1970), Propositions 5--6 and Lemma 7
(blueprint: lem-trf-linear-sections-hilbert-standard-degrees). -/
def linearSectionGradedMap {V : Type u} [CommRing V] [IsLocalRing V] {q : ℕ}
    (x : Fin q → IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V) :
    Ideal.associatedGraded (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V) →+
      Ideal.associatedGraded (linearSectionMaximalIdeal x) :=
  Ideal.associatedGradedMap (Ideal.Quotient.mk (linearSectionIdeal x))
    (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V) (linearSectionMaximalIdeal x) Ideal.le_comap_map

/-- The module quotient `E/(x_1*,...,x_q*)E` over the original tangent ring.
Source: Hironaka (1970), Lemma 7 and Remark (12.2)
(blueprint: lem-trf-linear-sections-hilbert-standard-degrees). -/
abbrev linearSectionInitialQuotient {V : Type u} [CommRing V] [IsLocalRing V] {q : ℕ}
    (x : Fin q → IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V) (b : Ideal V) : Type u :=
  (adicInitialIdeal (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V) b) ⧸
    ((Ideal.span (Set.range fun i ↦
        DirectSum.of (Ideal.associatedGradedPiece (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V)) 1
          (Submodule.Quotient.mk
            ⟨(x i).val, (pow_one (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V)).symm ▸ (x i).property⟩))) •
      (⊤ : Submodule (Ideal.associatedGraded (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V))
        (adicInitialIdeal (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V) b)))

/-- Linear sections bound the Hilbert--Samuel function; equality preserves the canonical
initial-ideal quotient and every minimal homogeneous generating family with its degrees.
All lengths are finite because the ideals are proper in Noetherian local rings.
The witness `hregular` supplies the induced local structure used in the final `nuStar`.

Source: Hironaka (1970), Propositions 5--6, pp.157--159, Lemma 7, p.160,
and the first part of Remark (12.2), p.167
(blueprint: lem-trf-linear-sections-hilbert-standard-degrees).

Proof (the node's ten steps):
1. Complete and permute the parameters. Regular-local-generators-regular-sequence gives
regularity of each successive quotient. Quotient-local-structure and surjective-image-
noetherian give nonzero Noetherian local quotients by the successive images of b.
2. Maximal-adic-graded-length-bridge gives finite lengths. Surjective restriction of
scalars identifies submodule lattices, hence their lengths. Length zero means zero.
3. For each section z, multiplication L/m^n → L/m^(n+1) has kernel
K_n = (m^(n+1):z)/m^n and cokernel B/(mB)^(n+1). Length additivity twice gives
h_L(n) = h_L(n-1) + h_B(n) - length K_n. Sum to get h_L ≤ Λ h_B, including n=0.
4. Iteration gives the bound. Equality of endpoints forces every nonnegative intermediate
gap to vanish: Λ^i δ(n) ≥ δ(n). The length formula then makes every K_n zero.
5. The colon identities show that the degree-one initial form t of z is injective on gr L.
6. In positive degree, lift a kernel class as a = zb + c with c in m^(r+1).
The colon identity forces b into m^(r-1). Degree zero is the residue-field identity.
Thus gr L/t gr L is canonically gr B.
7. Regular-hypersurface-initial-form identifies the ambient graded quotient by t with
the next regular tangent ring. Its quotient by the initial ideal is the cone of B.
8. Injectivity of t modulo E gives E ∩ tS = tE; thus the canonical map identifies
E/tE with the next initial ideal. Iterate to obtain the stated representative formula.
9. Since tE lies in S_+E, the minimal-generator quotients E/S_+E are preserved by this
map, degree by degree. A homogeneous generating family is minimal precisely when its
classes form a basis of that quotient. Hence every such family keeps its exact degrees.
10. Its degree-d dimension is the multiplicity in nuStar. Equality of all multiplicities
identifies the increasing sequences with their infinite tails. Empty sections give the
identity; the zero ideal has the empty family and the all-infinity sequence. -/
theorem linearSectionsHilbertStandardDegrees
    {V : Type u} [CommRing V] [IsRegularLocalRing V]
    (q : ℕ) (x : Fin q → IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V)
    (hx : ∃ t : List V, IsLocalRing.IsRegularSystemOfParameters t ∧
      ∃ positions : Fin q ↪ Fin t.length, ∀ i, t.get (positions i) = (x i).val)
    (b : Ideal V) (hb : b ≤ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V) :
    ∃ hregular : IsRegularLocalRing (linearSectionRing x),
      (∀ n : ℕ, quotientHilbertFunction (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V) b n ≤
        ((AlgebraicGeometry.HilbertSamuel.summation^[q])
          (quotientHilbertFunction (linearSectionMaximalIdeal x)
            (b.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (linearSectionIdeal x))))) n) ∧
      (quotientHilbertFunction (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V) b =
        (AlgebraicGeometry.HilbertSamuel.summation^[q])
          (quotientHilbertFunction (linearSectionMaximalIdeal x)
            (b.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (linearSectionIdeal x)))) →
        (∃ e : linearSectionInitialQuotient x b ≃+
            adicInitialIdeal (linearSectionMaximalIdeal x)
              (b.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (linearSectionIdeal x))),
          (∀ a : adicInitialIdeal (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V) b,
            (e (Submodule.Quotient.mk a)).val = linearSectionGradedMap x a.val) ∧
          (∀ (s : Ideal.associatedGraded (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V))
              (a : adicInitialIdeal (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V) b),
            (e (Submodule.Quotient.mk (s • a))).val =
              linearSectionGradedMap x s * (e (Submodule.Quotient.mk a)).val)) ∧
        (∀ (m : ℕ) (ξ : Fin m → Ideal.associatedGraded (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V))
            (d : Fin m → ℕ),
          IsMinimalGeneratingFamily (adicInitialIdeal (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V) b) ξ →
          HasDegrees (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal V) d ξ →
          IsMinimalGeneratingFamily
              (adicInitialIdeal (linearSectionMaximalIdeal x)
                (b.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (linearSectionIdeal x))))
              (fun i ↦ linearSectionGradedMap x (ξ i)) ∧
            HasDegrees (linearSectionMaximalIdeal x) d
              (fun i ↦ linearSectionGradedMap x (ξ i))) ∧
        nuStar b = @nuStar (linearSectionRing x) _ hregular.toIsLocalRing
          (b.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (linearSectionIdeal x)))) := by
  sorry

end Hironaka
